title The meter that cannot see a glob
prompt Keaton -- kg
think Followed my own recommendation: which other witness families does no pass run. Nearly re-derived a number the tree already keeps.
think My first count was 1901 witness files against 263 roster paths, and the naive gap of 1638 would have been wrong the same way the convergence denominator was wrong earlier this session -- a rostered choir calls many. Looked for the existing measurement instead and found it.
think witness_reach_scan reads 1,889 witnesses, 859 reached, 1,030 unreached, ceiling 1,093. So the front doors were one family among many, already tracked, with 63 of slack.
think Lowered the ceiling to the reading first, because slack in a ratchet is a quiet allowance to get worse: 63 witnesses could have fallen out of reach and every pass would still have read green.
think Then took the largest coherent unheard family in my own lane. tools/f carries 80 unheard, 45 of them the 5x7 font's glyph witnesses, with no choir. Timed one at 1.7s, so 45 is about 75 seconds -- affordable at cadence.
think Wrote the choir to DISCOVER its family rather than list it. A list goes stale the first lap somebody adds a glyph table, and it goes stale silently: the new witness never runs while the choir stays green covering less.
obs THREE FAULTS IN ONE LAP, and all three read exactly like a pass, which is why each is written into the file it bit. My glob assumed a middle segment and ran 44 of the 45, missing font5x7_witness.rish. The count read back from wc carried its newline, so sh received two lines and a family of 45 refused against a bound of 128. And my own control read argument $3 where the scan passes the path as $2, so a planted red looked like a pass -- the one direction a control must never fail in.
obs THE HONEST LIMIT: rostering the choir moved the reach meter by ONE while starting to run forty-five. The scan counts a witness reached when a rostered file NAMES it, and it cannot see a glob. Naming all forty-five would satisfy the number and restore the stale-list fault the discovery exists to prevent, so the run is kept and the number is explained beside the roster entry.
obs A meter that would be improved by making the code worse is a meter to read alongside the thing rather than instead of it.
obs Rostered fleet_rearm too: a guard this same session repaired and proved green, which nothing was running.
loom guard=witness_reach total=1889 reached=860 unreached=1029 ceiling_before=1093 ceiling_after=1029
loom choir=font5x7 members=45 seconds_each=1.7 control_behaviors=8 control_fail=0
rota lap 4381, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels, fifth lap by hand. What it surfaced: the boundary under the hand was between what a meter counts and what a program does, and the two parted cleanly for the first time this round.
file tools/f/font5x7_choir.rish one roster row for forty-five witnesses
